{
  "_about": [
    "Single source of truth for colours, fog, lights and post-processing. Code must not hard-code these.",
    "Top-level keys other than those starting with '_' are blocks. A level picks one with its \"palette\" field (or ?palette=<block>).",
    "Every block is merged over \"default\", so a block only lists what it changes.",
    "A block may hold \"presets\": { name: partial block }; ?preset=<name> picks one. \"defaultPreset\" names the one used when the URL gives none; a block with presets but no defaultPreset must be opened with ?preset=.",
    "Hex colours are sRGB, as seen in a colour picker. Angles are degrees, distances are metres.",
    "fog.color is the colour as it appears on screen: the renderer compensates for exposure, tone mapping and saturation. Every other colour is a surface or light colour and gets darker or lighter with exposure.",
    "accent is the one saturated colour of a chapter, used only on what the player must find. accent.intensity above 1 makes it glow (bloom) and read through fog."
  ],

